go.alis.build/sproto is deprecated in favour of go.alis.build/protodb/v2.

What it delivers: go get / go list -m -u show the module deprecation; gopls, staticcheck and
pkg.go.dev flag each package with its replacement.

Changes:
- go.mod: Go module deprecation comment directly above the module directive.
- Package docs end with a Deprecated paragraph: sproto -> protodb/v2 + spanneradapter,
  filtering -> protodb/v2/filtering, ordering -> protodb/v2/ordering. filtering and ordering
  had no package comment, so each gained a doc.go.
- READMEs open with a one-line deprecation notice.

Files: sproto/go.mod, sproto/docs.go, sproto/filtering/doc.go, sproto/ordering/doc.go,
sproto/README.md, sproto/filtering/README.md, sproto/ordering/README.md

Why: protodb/v2 absorbed sproto's filtering and ordering and already handles columns named after
SQL keywords; new work should use it. No behaviour change.
Checks: go doc prints each Deprecated paragraph; go mod edit -json shows Module.Deprecated;
go build ./... passes; gofmt clean on changed Go files.
